---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="What happens to your information when you visit this site or sign up for the newsletter.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Site Info" title="Privacy Policy" description="Last updated: September 2026" />
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <div class="prose max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-a:text-brand-700">
      <p>
        Hi neighbor! This page explains what happens to your information when you visit this site or sign up for
        the newsletter. We've tried to write it in plain English, because legal jargon doesn't help anybody.
      </p>
      <p>
        A quick reminder: this is a volunteer, resident-run project. We're not the HOA, and we're not affiliated
        with the Bent Grass Metropolitan District or Woodmen Hills Metropolitan District — just neighbors trying to
        keep other neighbors in the loop.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Right now, that's pretty simple: if you subscribe to the newsletter, we collect your email address so we
        can send it to you. That's it. We're not asking for anything else, we don't run ads, and we don't use
        tracking cookies to follow you around the internet.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do with it</h2>
      <p>
        We use your email to send you the newsletter you signed up for — nothing more. We will never sell, rent, or
        hand your information over to advertisers or outside companies. This is a neighborhood project, not a
        business.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your email address is stored in our own database (a Cloudflare D1 database, tied to this website) rather
        than handed to a separate newsletter platform when you sign up. We — the neighbor volunteers who run this
        site — are the only ones with access to it.
      </p>

      <h2>The tools behind this site</h2>
      <p>
        We want to be upfront about the technology running behind the scenes, since your information passes through
        these companies' systems, not just ours. Right now, we use:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare</a>, to host
          this website and store the subscriber list
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Older newsletter issues sent before we brought this in-house remain archived on{" "}
        <a href="https://buttondown.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buttondown</a>, the platform we used
        previously — see the <a href="/community-resources/monthly-newsletters">Monthly Newsletters</a> page.
      </p>
      <p>If our tooling changes again, we'll update this list right away. We're not going to quietly add new tools without telling you.</p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>Every newsletter email includes a one-click unsubscribe link — no questions asked, no account needed.</p>
      <p>Have a question or want something changed sooner? Just email us — see below.</p>

      <h2>A note on kids' information</h2>
      <p>
        We're not currently collecting information specifically about children. If that ever changes as this
        project grows, we'll update this policy to explain exactly how we'd handle it.
      </p>

      <h2>If things change</h2>
      <p>
        This is a small, evolving project, and it'll probably grow over time. Whenever we change how we handle your
        information, or add a new tool that touches it, we'll update this page and the date up top. If it's a
        bigger change, we'll mention it in the newsletter too, so nothing sneaks by quietly.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions?</h2>
      <p>
        We're your neighbors, so just reach out: <a href="mailto:bentgrassneighborhood@gmail.com">bentgrassneighborhood@gmail.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
